# Line endings.
#
# Git's default on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) converts text files to CRLF on
# checkout. For most of this repository that is harmless. For anything with a
# shebang it is fatal, and fatal in a way that reads as a broken toolchain
# rather than a line-ending problem:
#
#   $ ./scripts/dev-stack.sh
#   /usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory
#   /usr/bin/env: use -[v]S to pass options in shebang lines
#
# `bash\r` is not a program, so every one of the 22 shell scripts here — the
# local stack, the migrations, the backup, the restore drill, the first-run
# drill, the LAN HTTPS runbook — fails on a fresh Windows clone before it runs
# a single line. CI never saw it because CI is Ubuntu.
#
# So the scripts are checked out LF everywhere, whatever the platform and
# whatever the developer's core.autocrlf says. The .mjs entries are here for
# the same reason: scripts/dev-api.mjs and scripts/lint-css-hover.mjs both
# carry shebangs, and today they are only ever invoked as `node <file>` — which
# is exactly the kind of detail that changes quietly and breaks loudly.

* text=auto

*.sh  text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
